Error: Jet.UseAfterMove: `xs` was consumed by the binding `ys`, so it can't be used here
  --> Tests/UI/share_explicit_copies_use_after_move.jet:9:24
    |
  9 |     print("{ys.len()} {xs.len()}")
    |                        ^^
  --> Tests/UI/share_explicit_copies_use_after_move.jet:8:10
    |
  8 |     ys := xs
    |           ^^ `xs` moved to the binding `ys` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `xs` after the move, or give the binding `ys` a copy with `xs.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UseAfterMove
